+/* ---- 2252 (W8 survey): apps_smmu, read only, for the WLAN copy engines' streams ------------------------------------
+ * The live DT gives the WLAN node iommus = <&apps_smmu 0x1400 0x1>, so the copy engines' DMA arrives as stream 0x1400 or
+ * 0x1401, through the TBU whose range is 0x1400 to 0x17ff (pcie_qtb; pcie0 itself is disabled). Nothing in this kernel
+ * programs those streams. Every boot's ASTEROIDS USB probe lists the valid SMRs ABL leaves (0 to 4: 0x60, 0x540,
+ * 0x1c00/2, 0x40, 0x480) and sCR0 has USFCFG set, so a WLAN DMA today would be an unidentified-stream fault.
