+ * under this hypervisor. Global: sCR0 0x0, ID0-2 0x20-0x28, sGFSR 0x48 (ASTEROIDS USB, every boot). SMR 0x800+4n and S2CR
+ * 0xc00+4n for n below ID0's count (IPA's ipa_mmu_choose, 42 boots). CBAR 0x1000+4n and CBA2R 0x1800+4n, and for every
+ * bank SCTLR 0x0, TTBR0 0x20/0x24, TTBR1 0x28/0x2c and FSR 0x58 (IPA's CBsurvey, ast170, all 72 banks). TCR2 0x10, TCR
+ * 0x30, MAIR0 0x38 and MAIR1 0x3c (ipa_mmu_choose's saved set) only for a bank a WLAN SMR selects. Nothing is read past
+ * ID0's SMR count or ID1's bank count, and the tables are not read at all unless ID0, ID1 and ID2 are the values measured
+ * since ast159, because a different geometry is a different hypervisor build and none of these reads is proven there.
+ *
+ * Left out on purpose: sGFAR, sGFSYNR0-2, each bank's FAR and FSYNR, TLBSTATUS and ACTLR (never read on this phone, and
+ * the hypervisor emulates the global space: the boot shim once took an external abort reading SMR 7, cause unknown); the
+ * TBU at 0x16cd000 (never read, and its clock and power are not ours to assume); any write, including a fault clear. A
